{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q414445","formula":"AlN","hill":"AlN","elements":["N","Al"],"composition":{"N":1.0,"Al":1.0},"names":{"en":"Aluminum nitride","ru":"Нитрид алюминия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Aluminium nitride (AlN) is a solid nitride of aluminium, which was first synthesized in 1862 by F. Briegleb and A. Geuther. AlN is a wide-bandgap semiconductor composed of aluminium and nitrogen. It crystallizes predominantly in the wurtzite structure and exhibits a direct band gap of approximately 6 eV at room temperature The exceptionally wide bandgap enables applications in deep-ultraviolet optoelectronics, while the material's thermal conductivity 321 W/(m·K), and strong polarization effects make it an important buffer and template material for III-nitride quantum heterostructures used in high-power and high-frequency electronic devices.","ru":"Нитри́д алюми́ния (алюмонитри́д) — бинарное неорганическое химическое соединение алюминия с азотом."},"fame":28,"pubchemCid":90455,"mass":40.988,"charge":0,"smiles":"N#[Al]","inchikey":"PIGFYZPCRLYGLF-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"azanylidynealumane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-661","atoms":20,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.129,0.0,0.0],[-1.564,2.709,0.0],[0.0,0.0,5.017]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":1.564,"y":0.903,"z":2.505,"el":"Al"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.806,"z":0.0,"el":"Al"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.806,"z":5.017,"el":"Al"},{"x":1.564,"y":0.903,"z":4.418,"el":"N"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.806,"z":1.91,"el":"N"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.613,"z":2.505,"el":"Al"},{"x":-1.564,"y":4.516,"z":0.0,"el":"Al"},{"x":-1.564,"y":4.516,"z":5.017,"el":"Al"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.613,"z":4.418,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.564,"y":4.516,"z":1.91,"el":"N"},{"x":4.693,"y":0.903,"z":2.505,"el":"Al"},{"x":3.129,"y":1.806,"z":0.0,"el":"Al"},{"x":3.129,"y":1.806,"z":5.017,"el":"Al"},{"x